course: dictionary
lesson: 3432
title: Many meanings of eye
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word eye can mean different things, so use the context to decide which one it is. «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump, and even with its eyes shut it can see through notches in its eyelids.» Here eyes are the body parts we see with.
explain: Sometimes eye is part of a phrase, and then the meaning is not the body part. «Keep an eye on» means watch. In «The eye of a storm is the calm centre of a hurricane», eye means the middle. Ask yourself: what would fit here?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end.» Eye means the body part we see with, and the sentence still makes sense. If the swap sounds silly, try another meaning.
fact: An eye is the part of the body you see with, and a person has 2 eyes.
fact: The eye of a needle is the small hole the thread goes through.
fact: The eye of a storm is the calm centre of a hurricane.
fact: To eye something is to look at it closely, often because you want it.
fact: «Keep an eye on» means watch, and «see eye to eye» means agree.
exercise: «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end.» In this sentence, what is an eye? | To look at something closely | The calm middle of a storm | *A body part we see with | A small hole for thread
exercise: Mum says, «Can you keep an eye on the pasta?» What does keep an eye on mean? | *Watch | Cook it again | Forget | Eat it
exercise: «The eye of the storm was calm and still.» What does eye mean here? | A small hole | *The calm centre | A part of the body | To look at closely
test: «She has an eye for good pictures.» What does have an eye for mean? | To close one eye | To buy lots of pictures | *To be good at noticing them | To have a sore eye
test: How many eyes does a person have? | *2 | 1 | 4 | 3
exam: Which sentence uses eye as a verb, meaning to look at closely? | The needle had a tiny eye. | The storm had a calm eye. | Her eyes were bright and blue. | *He eyed the cake for a long time, wanting a slice.
